- ci/W-407-spec-12.log #1: closed — In prototype `Inbox.tsx`, `refreshInbox`'s catch now sets `EMPTY` only when `!hasSuccessfulLoadRef.current`. A later failure touches only `readFailed`, and selection, detail, detached state and reasons are left alone, so the `currentId`-undefined reopen-first path is gone. Served `w407.spec.ts` b6 (305ff) aborts one interval read at 1280 and 390 with the seventh item open and a half-typed ratio. Through failure and recovery it asserts 14 rows, `aria-selected`, the detail subject, the ratio value and focus, and list scroll. `w407-served-b6-r13.out` passes, and the mbox (`b47798ee…`, brief:11) postdates it. Brief:33, 65, 87 and 105 state it. Round-12 advisories #2 (no `studio` field, plus a server key test), #3 (1.4.11 named as not met; Defaults 2) and #4 (in-flight coalescing) are also addressed.

## Verdict
Revision g closes the round-12 blocker. A background failure no longer wipes the queue, and the input boundary stays sound. The new secondary labels, the shade-only focus with 1.4.11 named as an accepted trade-off, and the 72ch Default make sense on the r13 captures. What remains is three advisory gaps in the new refresh-retention states: the failure notice is not visible in the narrow list, the retained reading disappears when the queue empties, and an answered item is briefly shown as withdrawn.
VERDICT: PASS
